    "## Outer products and projectors  *(Book §7.6, Example 7.14)*\n",
    "\n",
    "A bra times a ket gives a scalar; a **ket times a bra** gives a matrix, the outer product $|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\phi|$ with entries $x_i y_j^{*}$. The important case is a basis state with itself: $|0\\rangle\\langle 0|$ and $|1\\rangle\\langle 1|$ are **projectors** — Hermitian, idempotent ($P^2=P$), and summing to the identity.\n",
    "\n",
    "They give a compact restatement of the Born rule: $P(0)=\\langle q|\\,(|0\\rangle\\langle 0|)\\,|q\\rangle=|\\langle 0|q\\rangle|^2=|x|^2$. Sandwich an outcome's projector between $\\langle q|$ and $|q\\rangle$ and you get its probability. This \"project, then take the norm\" form is what generalizes to the measurement operators used from Chapter 12 onward. Below we verify all three routes to $P(0)$ agree on the chapter's example, and build $|+\\rangle\\langle +|$."
   ]
  },
